{
  "action": "In general, a standard system update will make all the necessary changes.",
  "cves": [
    "CVE-2026-101258",
    "CVE-2026-103226",
    "https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2171528"
  ],
  "description": "Rick de Jager discovered that Ghostscript incorrectly handled memory\nunder certain circumstances when processing PostScript documents. If a\nuser or automated system were tricked into processing a specially crafted\ndocument, an attacker could possibly use this issue to bypass the sandbox\nand execute arbitrary code. (CVE-2026-101258)\n\nIt was discovered that Ghostscript incorrectly handled memory when\nconverting certain fonts. If a user or automated system were tricked into\nprocessing a specially crafted file, an attacker could possibly use this\nissue to cause Ghostscript to crash, or possibly execute arbitrary code.\n(CVE-2026-103226)\n\nPaulos Yibelo discovered that Ghostscript did not properly validate\ncertain operands when loading fonts. If a user or automated system were\ntricked into processing a specially crafted file, an attacker could\npossibly use this issue to bypass the sandbox and execute arbitrary code.\n(No CVE number)",
  "id": "USN-8949-1",
  "isummary": "Several security issues were fixed in Ghostscript.",
